From 3830693c6a6156a3cbcec03cc594612a9090e16f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: clover porter <clover@localhost>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:15:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 31/31] cpuidle: psci: create the cpuidle device after deferred
 probing

psci-cpuidle is a faux device created at device_initcall, and a faux
device cannot defer: if the CPU PM domains are not there yet, every CPU
fails ("CPU 0 failed to PSCI idle", "Failed to create psci-cpuidle
device") and the system runs with no idle states at all.

That happens when a CPU PM domain has a parent provided by a later
driver. On clover the APSS system-sleep domain sits under the MPM (as on
agatti): psci-cpuidle-domain deferred at 0.06 s, the MPM probed at
0.8 s, psci-cpuidle gave up at 1.0 s, and the domains appeared at 1.15 s.

Create the device at late_initcall_sync instead, after the deferred
probes have been flushed.
---
 drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
index dcf20ea5e..3c489ce87 100644
--- a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
@@ -489,4 +489,4 @@ static int __init psci_idle_init(void)
 
 	return 0;
 }
-device_initcall(psci_idle_init);
+late_initcall_sync(psci_idle_init);
